346 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (     The core objective of this application is to exhibit how OOPS principles such as encapsulation, inheritance, polymorphism, and abstraction can be utilized effectively within a single cohesive system. Encapsulation is applied to protect property-related data and restrict direct manipulation through controlled access methods. Inheritance is used to create hierarchical relationships among classes, allowing common features to be shared while enabling specialization in derived classes. Polymorphism supports dynamic behavior during runtime, enabling different property types to override methods and provide distinct outputs based on user interactions. Abstraction is implemented through generalized classes and interfaces that outline essential behavior while hiding unnecessary complexity, ensuring cleaner and more flexible code.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
