381 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Technically, many conventional systems lack structured design and modular, object-oriented principles, resulting in rigid architectures that are hard to maintain, modify, or extend. Legacy real estate platforms often struggle to incorporate new property types or recommendation features without extensive code changes. The lack of object-oriented modeling also reduces the value of such systems for educational purposes, where understanding concepts like modularity, inheritance, encapsulation, and polymorphism is crucial.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [5 6]
>>
endobj
382 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (    Given these limitations, there is a clear need for a well-structured property recommendation system capable of categorizing property types, modeling their attributes effectively, and providing truly meaningful recommendations. The proposed Property Recommendation System, implemented using Java and OOPS principles, addresses these challenges by organizing properties into hierarchical classes, using polymorphism for category-specific details, and ensuring secure data handling.)
/Pg 13 0 R
>>
endobj
