/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (3.2 Recommendation Mechanism      The recommendation mechanism implemented in this system follows a structured, rule-based approach rather than complex machine-learning forecasting. When the user selects a category \(such as residential or commercial\), the system evaluates the available objects within that category and displays the most relevant or featured properties.       The mechanism uses method overriding to display category-specific recommendations. For instance, residential properties may highlight features such as number of bedrooms or furnishing status, whereas commercial properties may prioritize shop/office suitability or floor space. This dynamic behavior allows each property type to present distinctive details. Recommendation Flow Process:)
/E (3.2 Recommendation Mechanism      The recommendation mechanism implemented in this system follows a structured, rule-based approach rather than complex machine-learning forecasting. When the user selects a category \(such as residential or commercial\), the system evaluates the available objects within that category and displays the most relevant or featured properties.       The mechanism uses method overriding to display category-specific recommendations. For instance, residential properties may highlight features such as number of bedrooms or furnishing status, whereas commercial properties may prioritize shop/office suitability or floor space. This dynamic behavior allows each property type to present distinctive details. Recommendation Flow Process:)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [0 1]
>>
